/*
    Currency conversion calculation group (requirement #4).
    Group controller wants to switch local <-> USD, with sales using the
    monthly-average rate and stock valuation using the month-end rate.

    Calculation Group: "Currency View"
    Precedence: 20 (apply AFTER Time Intelligence, so YTD/PY context is already
    set before conversion — converting first then summing periods would use
    the wrong day's rate for YTD-style sums)
    Column: "Currency Selection"
*/

-- Calculation Item: "Local" (no conversion, base case)
SELECTEDMEASURE ()

-- Calculation Item: "USD (Monthly Avg Rate)" -- use for P&L / sales measures
SUMX (
    VALUES ( 'Dim Date'[CalendarMonth] ),
    VAR MonthRate =
        CALCULATE (
            AVERAGE ( 'Fact ExchangeRate'[RateToUSD_MonthAvg] )
        )
    RETURN
        SELECTEDMEASURE () * MonthRate
)

-- Calculation Item: "USD (Month-End Rate)" -- use for stock/balance-sheet measures
VAR EndRate =
    CALCULATE (
        AVERAGE ( 'Fact ExchangeRate'[RateToUSD_EOD] ),
        LASTDATE ( 'Dim Date'[Date] )
    )
RETURN
    SELECTEDMEASURE () * EndRate

/*
    Why this needs per-month iteration for the average-rate item: a quarter or
    year filter context covers multiple months, each with its own monthly
    average rate. Converting the whole period's local total by a single rate
    would be wrong - the P&L convention is "convert each month's result at
    that month's average rate, then sum the USD amounts." SUMX over
    VALUES(CalendarMonth) enforces that.

    The month-end item deliberately does NOT iterate by month - stock value
    is a point-in-time balance (semi-additive, see measures_inventory.dax),
    so it converts at the rate on the LAST date in the filter context, not
    an average across months.

    Usage: [Net Revenue] sliced by "USD (Monthly Avg Rate)" gives Group
    Controller the Sales-relevant USD figure. [Closing Stock Value] sliced by
    "USD (Month-End Rate)" gives the balance-sheet-relevant figure. Same
    calculation group, correct rate convention picked per measure type by
    which item the report uses - not hardcoded per measure.
*/
